 "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/23/2023", "sessionEndDt": "05/20/2023", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "BR Consulting educates students on consulting through work on a project with a local company, non-profit or alumni run small company.\u00a0 The seven directors act as the partners of a consulting firm.\u00a0 Through this process they learn the aspects of running a consulting business and how to be a manager or above on a project.\u00a0 There are weekly meetings with the faculty for education, managing the business and reviewing consulting students projects.\u00a0 The student consultants apply in the fall to be a consultant.\u00a0 They take responsibility for finalizing the consulting project, conducting the work and delivering a final recommendation in the spring before graduation.\u00a0 There are six just in time education sessions timed to the specific point in their project.\u00a0 In addition, there a regular meetings with the directors and faculty.\u00a0 The students present their interim findings before winter break. Before they deliver the final presentation, there are multiple reviews and a case competition.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: Johnson and graduate students by permission of Faculty.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GM", "acadGroup": "BU", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2839, "crseId": 364299, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "NMI", "catalogNbr": "5090", "titleShort": "Big Red MicroEnterprise", "titleLong": "Big Red MicroEnterprise", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "IND", "ssrComponentLong": "Independent Study", "section": "001", "classNbr": 8350, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/09/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "mm462", "firstName": "Mark", "middleName": "B.", "lastName": "Milstein"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": null, "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": null, "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "By permission only"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/20/2023", "addConsent": "D", "addConsentDescr": "Department Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "IS", "instrModeDescrshort": "Indp Stds", "instrModeDescr": "Independent Studies", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 0.5, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["IND"], "gradingBasis": "SUI", "gradingBasisShort": "S/U NoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Satisfactory/Unsatisfactory (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/23/2023", "sessionEndDt": "05/20/2023", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "Big Red Microenterprise (BRM) is a student-managed, experiential learning opportunity overseen by the Center for Sustainable Global Enterprise where graduate student coaches work with promising, but underserved, entrepreneurs in the local community to support inclusive wealth creation and economic development. Launched in 2009, BRM is a unique program which allows students to develop critical general management skills through engagement of real local companies that face acute operational and financial challeng